      "standard": "W1.a",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "question_html": "Simplify. Rewrite with positive exponents only: \\( (4x^3)^2 \\cdot 2x^{-4} \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "q1",
          "type": "radio",
          "label": "",
          "options": [
            { "value": "A", "text": "\\( 32x^2 \\)" },
            { "value": "B", "text": "\\( 16x^6 \\)" },
            { "value": "C", "text": "\\( 32x^6 \\)" },
            { "value": "D", "text": "\\( 8x^2 \\)" }
          ],
          "answer": "A"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Power rule first: (ab)^n = a^n * b^n. Then multiply by adding exponents.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "(4x^3)^2 · 2x^(-4)",
        "= 4^2 · x^6 · 2x^(-4)     [power rule]",
        "= 16 · 2 · x^(6 + (-4))    [product rule: add exponents]",
        "= 32x^2"
      ],
      "feedback_correct": "🔥 Exponent rules applied correctly.",
      "feedback_wrong": "Apply power rule to (4x^3)^2 first: 4^2 = 16, (x^3)^2 = x^6. Then multiply: 16 · 2 · x^(6-4) = 32x^2."
    },
    {
