      "section": "A",
      "standard": "W1.b",
      "type": "fractional-exp",
      "question_html": "Rewrite as a radical expression, then evaluate without a calculator: \\( 27^{2/3} \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "q2_value",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "27^(2/3) =",
          "answer": 9,
          "tolerance": 0.01
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Denominator of fractional exponent is the root, numerator is the power. a^(m/n) = (nth root of a)^m.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "27^(2/3) = (cbrt(27))^2     [denominator 3 = cube root]",
        "= 3^2                        [cbrt(27) = 3]",
        "= 9"
      ],
      "feedback_correct": "🔥 Rational exponent converted and evaluated.",
      "feedback_wrong": "The denominator 3 means cube root. cbrt(27) = 3. Then square it: 3^2 = 9."
    },
